      "abstract": "In current times, Credit card fraud faces a significant issue to banking systems, need accurate and real-time detection of both relational fraud patterns and individual anomalous transactions. However, existing Graph Neural Network (GNN) to detect relational fraud patterns across entities and autoencoder to identify anomalous transactions struggles from independent training, absence of temporal pattern modeling and deficiency of context-aware anomaly. Therefore, an integrated Temporal GNN-Autoencoder (TGNNAE) framework is proposed. Primarily, transaction data is collected from banking systems consisting transaction logs, entity metadata and confirmed fraud labels. Then, data is preprocessed using min-max scaling, categorical attributes and temporal coding. Then, temporal transaction graph constructed and managed using TGNN to produce graph and time-aware embeddings for each transaction. Now, these embeddings fed to attention-based autoencoder to reconstruct embedding patterns and compute anomaly scores. Simultaneously, classification head process GNN embeddings to output fraud probabilities. Moreover, fusion layer combines fraud probability and anomaly score into a single fraud risk score. Further, TGNN and AE are integrated through fusion layer which are trained for utilizing loss function to optimizes both accuracy and anomaly score allowing accurate and real-time fraud detection. Finally, integrated TGNN-AE achieved better results in terms of accuracy (89.25%) and precision (94.76%) respectively when compared with GNN.",
